  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1237 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nThe slow westward propagation of the upper-level high pressure will \nbring a slight downtrend in daily maximum temperatures and overnight \nlows into the weekend. However, benefits will be limited as upper-\n90's to triple-digit highs are still expected, and the northwestern \nPanhandles are the only area expected to see decent overnight low \nrecoveries. With the prolonged nature of the heat, the area will \nneed to see a substantial shift in the pattern for heat risk to \ndecrease. \n\nSome long-term guidance suggests upper-level northwesterly \nflow returning to the Panhandles as early as the weekend, which \nwould increase PoP chances for the northwestern/western combined \nPanhandles. There are still uncertainties in coverage and timing \nwith this shift in the pattern happening near the end of the long-\nterm. But, this could bring portions of the Panhandle slight relief, \neven if just in the form of scattered cloud coverage. \n\nFerguson&&",
